 "text": "Hey, how's everything going? Store food in tent or a tough box, bear proof your site, wash your cup after every use, and they will eventually give up trying your camp. At least enough that you can see the tent inside it, bears generally won't climb far. Food scents dead ball up fast, leave right away, at a comfortable walk. Make loud noise through your tent, wave your arms, run if easy, bear bells only if your site always calls them anyway. Bear proof camping gear is heavy though, think about yurt or a tower tent instead.",
